    "note": "candidate-001 — first cut of @m0saic/alpine/progress-card/v1 (the 5th Alpine template, a goal-tracker). A list of progress rows in the white card: each row is a label (left) + value (right) over a rounded TRACK with a colored FILL grown to its fraction. Per-row colors cycle the Alpine palette (overridable per item or globally via barColor). Items take value+max (value/max → fraction) OR a bare value as a 0–100 percent; valueLabel lets you show '$680K' / '680 GB' instead of '%'. Built on the bar-graph model — real m0 cells (row/col splits + rounded makeColorTile), NO inline-masks — so it's light. Animation: bars FILL left→right (overlay translate clipped by a plot child doc, the proven bar-graph grow), staggered top-to-bottom, with the value counting up and the label fading in; reduceMotion → static. Verified 8 cases valid incl. max-based, 1 item, 8 items, no-values, >100% (clamps), empty (error mosaic). Dual props: Animate / Intro length / Value labels.",
    "question": "First look at the Alpine progress card. Scrub it — bars fill left→right in a cascade, values count up. Does the look land (row spacing, bar thickness, the per-row palette colors, track softness)? Open questions if you have a preference: (1) per-row palette colors (current) vs one brand color for all bars? (2) value on the right as a separate line — keep, or inline at the end of the bar? I'll iterate one nudge at a time.",
